        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Online sources are less predictable. In addition to the above information, record at least the URL and the access date, as well as any other information that might help you identify the source for readers.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                355,
                772,
                431
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    355.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    355.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    431.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    431.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. Record quotations exactly. Copy quotations exactly as they appear in the original, down to every comma and semicolon. If the quotation is long, photocopy it, cut-and-paste it, or download the entire source.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                442,
                771,
                520
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    442.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    442.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    520.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    520.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. Mark quotations and paraphrases unambiguously as the words of others. This is crucial: take notes so that weeks or months later you cannot possibly think that words and ideas from a source are your own. Whether you take notes on paper or on a computer, always highlight or use a different font to distinguish direct quotations. Then distinguish paraphrases and summaries another way. Prominent scholars have been humiliated by accusations of plagiarism because—they claimed—they did not clearly mark words they copied or paraphrased, then “forgot” they were not their own.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                533,
                772,
                741
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    533.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    533.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    741.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    741.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. Don't paraphrase too closely. When you paraphrase a source in your notes, you must do more than merely replace words in the source with synonyms. That is also considered plagiarism, even if you cite the source. You must recast the entire passage in your own language, which includes using your own sentence structure. For example, the first paraphrase below is plagiarism because it tracks the structure of the original almost word for word. The second paraphrase is paraphrased appropriately.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                753,
                773,
                936
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    753.0
                ],
                [
                    773.0,
                    753.0
                ],
                [
                    773.0,
